{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7f6c4a1e-9b2d-4e5f-8a3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c",
    "name": "Mental Health API",
    "description": "REST API for the Mental Health platform.\n\nBase URL: `{{baseUrl}}`\n\n## Authentication\n\n- `Register` and `Login` return an `accessToken` (JWT) and a `refreshToken`.\n- The `accessToken` must be sent as a `Bearer` token in the `Authorization` header for protected routes (auto-applied to the whole collection). `Login`, `Register`, and `Refresh Tokens` opt out of the automatic header.\n- The `refreshToken` is sent in the **request body** of the `POST /auth/refresh` endpoint. Do **not** send the `accessToken` in the `Authorization` header on the refresh call — the refresh strategy validates any Bearer header against the *refresh* secret, so the access token there would cause a 401.\n- An automated Postman script saves both tokens into the collection variables `accessToken` and `refreshToken` after Register/Login/Refresh.\n\n## Workflow order\n\n1. `Register` (or `Login`)\n2. `User` and `Profile` endpoints (get/update profile, update settings) require an access token\n3. `Check-ins` (get history / create a daily check-in — kept unique per day, drives the streak)\n4. `Journal` (list / create entries)\n5. `Refresh Tokens` (rotate tokens) / `Logout` (revoke refresh tokens)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "auth": {
            "type": "noauth"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has accessToken and refreshToken', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"jane.doe@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\",\n  \"name\": \"Jane Doe\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new user and returns the user profile along with an access token and refresh token."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "auth": {
            "type": "noauth"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has accessToken and refreshToken', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"jane.doe@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticates a user with email and password and returns an access token and refresh token."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Tokens",
          "auth": {
            "type": "noauth"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('New token pair returned and saved', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges a valid, non-revoked refresh token for a new access token / refresh token pair (rotation — the old token is revoked). The refresh token is sent in the **request body**. This request disables the automatic Bearer header: the refresh strategy validates any Authorization header token against the refresh secret, so the access token must not be sent here (it would cause a 401)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Logout message returned', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.message).to.eql('Logged out successfully');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes all active refresh tokens for the authenticated user. Requires a valid Bearer access token (auto-applied from the `accessToken` collection variable)."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
